 "reading": "MDE = smallest accuracy gap on a 0.005 grid whose exact two-sided McNemar power reaches the target, given a discordance rate d; power is monotone in the gap at fixed n and d, so this is the first crossing (the discrete sawtooth is in the number of discordant pairs, not in the gap). Each n's MDE range covers a different d range (table.headline_by_n): n = 30 has no MDE at d 0.2, so compare n = 30 and n = 60 over d 0.3-0.5 (common_discordance_range_n30_n60). REV-B (reports/orchestration/review/S176_REV-B_eval_governance.md Q26) reported about 0.28-0.33 at n = 30 and 0.16-0.24 at n = 60 for 80 % power under its own discordance grid. H1 needs two such tests (B4 > B1 and B4 > B2): the joint power is only bounded (Frechet) because both share B4's answers.",
